WEBVTT

00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:45.842
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:46.149 --> 00:02:50.518
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:50.787 --> 00:02:53.221
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:53.523 --> 00:02:58.358
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:58.628 --> 00:03:01.791
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:02.031 --> 00:03:06.559
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:06.836 --> 00:03:14.004
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.379
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:19.649 --> 00:03:22.709
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:22.919 --> 00:03:27.219
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:31.426
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:31.694 --> 00:03:35.186
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:35.431 --> 00:03:38.923
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:39.202 --> 00:03:43.070
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:43.339 --> 00:03:47.105
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:47.443 --> 00:03:53.075
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:53.282 --> 00:03:59.448
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:03:59.722 --> 00:04:03.590
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:03.793 --> 00:04:08.287
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:13.297
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:13.536 --> 00:04:21.307
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:22.378 --> 00:04:27.543
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:36.715
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:18.774 --> 00:09:23.734
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:24.013 --> 00:09:28.677
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:30.886 --> 00:09:32.945
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:33.189 --> 00:09:35.817
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:36.892 --> 00:09:38.189
She's missing again.

00:09:39.128 --> 00:09:41.494
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:41.731 --> 00:09:44.791
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:47.797
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:48.003 --> 00:09:50.233
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:50.539 --> 00:09:53.133
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:58.414 --> 00:09:59.711
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:09:59.982 --> 00:10:02.542
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:02.818 --> 00:10:06.049
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:06.255 --> 00:10:10.316
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:10.559 --> 00:10:13.426
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:13.662 --> 00:10:17.996
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:18.234 --> 00:10:21.670
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:21.937 --> 00:10:24.428
Children, children.

00:10:24.907 --> 00:10:28.866
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:29.512 --> 00:10:32.504
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:32.748 --> 00:10:38.050
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:38.287 --> 00:10:41.347
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:41.557 --> 00:10:44.617
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:45.594 --> 00:10:48.688
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:48.931 --> 00:10:51.456
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:51.767 --> 00:10:55.328
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:55.538 --> 00:10:58.473
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:58.707 --> 00:11:00.299
Exactly what I say.

00:11:00.776 --> 00:11:03.244
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:03.446 --> 00:11:05.141
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:05.815 --> 00:11:09.979
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:10.619 --> 00:11:15.113
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:15.391 --> 00:11:19.987
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:20.229 --> 00:11:22.220
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:22.465 --> 00:11:24.729
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.332
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:29.595
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:29.972 --> 00:11:34.671
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:39.347
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:39.849 --> 00:11:42.340
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:42.618 --> 00:11:43.949
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:48.779
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.596
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:55.865 --> 00:11:59.665
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:11:59.969 --> 00:12:03.302
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:03.839 --> 00:12:04.931
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:05.174 --> 00:12:06.505
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:08.143 --> 00:12:11.874
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:12.147 --> 00:12:15.605
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:16.018 --> 00:12:19.715
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:20.289 --> 00:12:23.781
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:24.026 --> 00:12:28.122
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:28.631 --> 00:12:34.160
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:39.831
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:44.402
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:44.713 --> 00:12:48.149
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:51.683
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:52.054 --> 00:12:53.885
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:54.089 --> 00:12:55.420
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:55.824 --> 00:12:59.487
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:12:59.695 --> 00:13:02.994
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:03.566 --> 00:13:07.093
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:10.230
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:10.439 --> 00:13:14.341
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:15.077 --> 00:13:19.013
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:19.248 --> 00:13:22.945
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:23.252 --> 00:13:26.744
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:27.022 --> 00:13:29.013
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:29.258 --> 00:13:30.885
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:35.091
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:35.364 --> 00:13:38.856
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:39.068 --> 00:13:43.402
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:43.639 --> 00:13:47.735
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:47.943 --> 00:13:53.779
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:09.732 --> 00:14:16.501
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:17.406 --> 00:14:23.811
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:35.624 --> 00:14:37.615
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:50.205 --> 00:14:51.832
Come here, my child.

00:14:58.347 --> 00:14:59.712
Now sit down.

00:15:00.649 --> 00:15:04.210
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:04.486 --> 00:15:07.455
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:07.856 --> 00:15:09.824
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:10.059 --> 00:15:12.289
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:12.961 --> 00:15:14.189
If you'll feel better.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.496
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:17.733 --> 00:15:21.533
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:21.804 --> 00:15:26.298
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:26.508 --> 00:15:28.533
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:28.811 --> 00:15:31.041
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:31.313 --> 00:15:34.146
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:34.349 --> 00:15:36.647
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:37.419 --> 00:15:40.388
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:40.656 --> 00:15:42.419
...and look in your garden.

00:15:42.658 --> 00:15:45.593
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:46.929 --> 00:15:50.558
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:50.766 --> 00:15:52.927
I was singing out there today.

00:15:53.602 --> 00:15:57.629
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.865
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:16:00.075 --> 00:16:02.407
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:02.678 --> 00:16:04.942
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.613
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:06.882 --> 00:16:09.248
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:09.451 --> 00:16:13.353
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:13.722 --> 00:16:17.214
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:19.895 --> 00:16:21.055
Maria...

00:16:22.064 --> 00:16:25.056
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:30.033
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:31.373 --> 00:16:33.773
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:33.976 --> 00:16:35.705
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:35.944 --> 00:16:38.606
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:39.281 --> 00:16:43.081
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:45.921 --> 00:16:47.047
Maria...

00:16:48.557 --> 00:16:51.321
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:51.593 --> 00:16:53.083
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:53.595 --> 00:16:55.927
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:56.165 --> 00:17:00.431
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:01.103 --> 00:17:04.129
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:04.339 --> 00:17:09.242
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:09.511 --> 00:17:12.241
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:12.447 --> 00:17:16.747
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:20.289 --> 00:17:21.517
Yes, Mother.

00:17:23.625 --> 00:17:25.286
If it is God's will.

00:17:27.529 --> 00:17:32.660
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:32.868 --> 00:17:35.098
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:35.771 --> 00:17:36.760
Seven children?!

00:17:37.005 --> 00:17:38.267
Do you like children?

00:17:39.041 --> 00:17:40.872
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:45.173
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:45.714 --> 00:17:47.113
Captain?

00:17:47.816 --> 00:17:52.651
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:52.888 --> 00:17:55.618
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:55.824 --> 00:18:00.124
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:00.896 --> 00:18:03.194
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:04.566 --> 00:18:07.501
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:44.373 --> 00:18:46.841
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:47.042 --> 00:18:49.567
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:51.914 --> 00:18:56.908
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:57.119 --> 00:18:59.349
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:05.861 --> 00:19:09.957
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:10.799 --> 00:19:13.063
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:14.636 --> 00:19:17.730
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:21.034
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:21.243 --> 00:19:24.303
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:30.816
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:31.153 --> 00:19:34.213
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:34.489 --> 00:19:38.050
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:38.293 --> 00:19:41.490
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:41.797 --> 00:19:47.895
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:54.241
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:54.476 --> 00:19:57.309
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:19:59.848 --> 00:20:02.476
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:02.751 --> 00:20:05.584
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:05.854 --> 00:20:09.017
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:10.092 --> 00:20:15.086
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:15.998 --> 00:20:19.832
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:20.102 --> 00:20:23.003
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:23.271 --> 00:20:24.966
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:25.207 --> 00:20:27.869
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:28.143 --> 00:20:31.943
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:32.147 --> 00:20:37.551
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:37.786 --> 00:20:41.051
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:41.323 --> 00:20:44.383
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:44.626 --> 00:20:48.062
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:48.296 --> 00:20:51.561
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:51.833 --> 00:20:55.064
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:55.337 --> 00:20:58.636
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:58.874 --> 00:21:02.173
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:02.411 --> 00:21:05.539
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:05.814 --> 00:21:09.079
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:09.317 --> 00:21:12.411
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:12.654 --> 00:21:18.092
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:19.661 --> 00:21:22.391
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:22.664 --> 00:21:25.758
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:26.001 --> 00:21:28.868
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:29.171 --> 00:21:32.197
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:32.507 --> 00:21:35.567
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:35.844 --> 00:21:38.870
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:39.114 --> 00:21:42.447
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:42.717 --> 00:21:45.584
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:45.887 --> 00:21:48.879
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:49.124 --> 00:21:52.025
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:52.227 --> 00:21:57.028
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:11.646 --> 00:22:13.273
Oh, help.

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:32.127
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:32.934 --> 00:22:37.735
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:38.006 --> 00:22:44.809
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:51.353 --> 00:22:53.753
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:56.591 --> 00:22:58.422
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:23:00.095 --> 00:23:03.326
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:07.097
Well, how do you do?

00:23:17.612 --> 00:23:21.673
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:48.036 --> 00:24:52.132
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:53.308 --> 00:24:54.775
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:02.717 --> 00:25:07.950
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:09.157 --> 00:25:12.217
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:12.927 --> 00:25:13.985
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:14.329 --> 00:25:15.591
Turn.

00:25:18.767 --> 00:25:19.927
Hat off.

00:25:23.138 --> 00:25:25.766
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:26.074 --> 00:25:27.632
But I don't have another.

00:25:27.909 --> 00:25:30.776
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:31.012 --> 00:25:32.274
What about this one?

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:33.811
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:39.142
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:40.422 --> 00:25:42.686
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:43.425 --> 00:25:44.949
Today, if possible.

00:25:45.927 --> 00:25:47.690
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:47.929 --> 00:25:50.659
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:50.932 --> 00:25:53.492
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:53.702 --> 00:25:56.170
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:56.371 --> 00:25:58.601
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:58.840 --> 00:26:00.671
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:02.377 --> 00:26:04.971
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:06.448 --> 00:26:10.851
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:11.119 --> 00:26:16.056
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:16.991 --> 00:26:18.788
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:19.027 --> 00:26:22.519
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:22.797 --> 00:26:25.493
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:27.361
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:27.569 --> 00:26:28.536
When do they play?

00:26:28.737 --> 00:26:32.798
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:33.041 --> 00:26:35.976
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:56.624 --> 00:27:57.784
Now...

00:27:58.393 --> 00:28:01.328
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:02.997 --> 00:28:04.988
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:09.498
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:10.805 --> 00:28:12.170
Liesl.

00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:14.169
Friedrich.

00:28:14.442 --> 00:28:15.966
Louisa.

00:28:16.244 --> 00:28:17.506
Kurt.

00:28:17.745 --> 00:28:18.803
Brigitta.

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:20.308
Marta.

00:28:26.688 --> 00:28:28.019
Gretl.

00:28:32.660 --> 00:28:36.096
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:36.331 --> 00:28:38.697
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:38.967 --> 00:28:42.425
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:42.637 --> 00:28:45.800
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:46.040 --> 00:28:48.804
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:49.043 --> 00:28:50.772
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:50.979 --> 00:28:52.640
The children will help you.

00:28:54.682 --> 00:28:58.675
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:28:59.554 --> 00:29:01.351
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:02.223 --> 00:29:03.781
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:03.992 --> 00:29:06.620
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:06.895 --> 00:29:08.954
And definitely not for me.

00:29:09.197 --> 00:29:11.825
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:12.634 --> 00:29:17.833
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:18.139 --> 00:29:19.231
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:30.351 --> 00:29:31.909
I don't know your signal.

00:29:33.388 --> 00:29:36.016
You may call me "captain."

00:29:48.937 --> 00:29:50.404
At ease.

00:29:53.207 --> 00:29:54.765
Now that there's just us...

00:29:55.043 --> 00:29:59.207
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:29:59.681 --> 00:30:03.674
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:04.452 --> 00:30:07.512
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:09.691 --> 00:30:13.457
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:13.761 --> 00:30:15.422
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:15.697 --> 00:30:19.189
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:19.634 --> 00:30:21.101
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:22.937 --> 00:30:26.930
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:27.609 --> 00:30:29.873
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:30.111 --> 00:30:32.875
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:33.114 --> 00:30:36.880
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:37.218 --> 00:30:39.846
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:40.054 --> 00:30:42.318
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:42.590 --> 00:30:45.286
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:45.560 --> 00:30:48.154
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:48.429 --> 00:30:51.557
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:51.799 --> 00:30:55.667
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:57.839 --> 00:31:01.138
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:01.409 --> 00:31:02.774
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:03.978 --> 00:31:05.502
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:07.915 --> 00:31:09.075
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:09.984 --> 00:31:11.679
And you're five years old?

00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:14.111
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:16.624 --> 00:31:19.650
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:21.095 --> 00:31:23.859
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:24.132 --> 00:31:25.497
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:26.467 --> 00:31:30.995
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:31.205 --> 00:31:33.002
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:33.207 --> 00:31:35.505
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:36.177 --> 00:31:38.270
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:38.513 --> 00:31:41.311
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:41.516 --> 00:31:44.883
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:45.687 --> 00:31:47.678
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:47.889 --> 00:31:49.789
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:49.991 --> 00:31:51.288
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:51.526 --> 00:31:54.723
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:54.962 --> 00:31:56.020
How do you do.

00:31:56.230 --> 00:31:59.131
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:10.211 --> 00:32:11.974
Poor little dears.

00:32:24.692 --> 00:32:29.061
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:42.910 --> 00:32:44.241
Good evening.

00:32:45.680 --> 00:32:49.241
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:56.457 --> 00:32:58.084
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:58.292 --> 00:33:01.022
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:04.562
No.

00:33:06.200 --> 00:33:07.462
Rheumatism.

00:33:17.278 --> 00:33:20.441
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:28.656 --> 00:33:31.625
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:32.160 --> 00:33:34.094
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:38.633 --> 00:33:40.567
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:40.768 --> 00:33:43.760
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:47.275 --> 00:33:49.072
What gift?

00:33:52.180 --> 00:33:54.341
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:54.615 --> 00:33:58.244
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:58.619 --> 00:34:00.587
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:00.822 --> 00:34:03.256
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:03.457 --> 00:34:06.517
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:06.794 --> 00:34:10.992
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:11.265 --> 00:34:13.460
...so warm and happy...

00:34:13.668 --> 00:34:15.431
...and pleasant.

00:34:24.679 --> 00:34:26.704
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:39.126 --> 00:34:40.150
Fräulein...

00:34:40.394 --> 00:34:44.228
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:44.465 --> 00:34:49.027
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:49.237 --> 00:34:50.898
...of indigestion?

00:34:52.473 --> 00:34:55.340
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:14.095 --> 00:35:16.757
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:17.031 --> 00:35:19.761
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:21.402 --> 00:35:23.836
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:24.038 --> 00:35:26.199
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:28.772
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:29.043 --> 00:35:30.840
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:31.579 --> 00:35:32.671
Certainly.

00:35:44.358 --> 00:35:46.053
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:48.896 --> 00:35:50.727
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:51.032 --> 00:35:53.057
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:55.403 --> 00:35:57.132
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:58.105 --> 00:36:02.565
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:02.877 --> 00:36:05.311
Not again, Father!

00:36:09.216 --> 00:36:11.275
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:11.919 --> 00:36:13.386
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:13.587 --> 00:36:17.148
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:18.125 --> 00:36:20.059
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:21.829 --> 00:36:25.663
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:25.967 --> 00:36:30.836
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:34.137
And Uncle Max.

00:36:34.408 --> 00:36:36.808
Uncle Max!

00:36:52.860 --> 00:36:54.191
Rolfe!

00:36:57.264 --> 00:36:58.322
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:00.868 --> 00:37:03.803
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:04.038 --> 00:37:06.700
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:06.941 --> 00:37:08.806
Yes, of course.

00:37:09.010 --> 00:37:11.808
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:12.046 --> 00:37:15.880
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:16.150 --> 00:37:20.052
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:20.321 --> 00:37:24.485
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:24.692 --> 00:37:28.150
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:28.829 --> 00:37:32.458
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:32.700 --> 00:37:34.895
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:35.136 --> 00:37:39.664
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:39.874 --> 00:37:41.307
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:41.509 --> 00:37:44.273
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:44.478 --> 00:37:47.140
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:49.517 --> 00:37:51.542
Will there be any reply?

00:37:52.820 --> 00:37:54.981
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:55.990 --> 00:37:59.084
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:00.828 --> 00:38:04.662
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:04.932 --> 00:38:07.332
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:08.235 --> 00:38:09.429
Well, let's see...

00:38:12.440 --> 00:38:14.408
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:15.409 --> 00:38:20.039
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:20.948 --> 00:38:24.247
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:24.518 --> 00:38:27.681
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:27.888 --> 00:38:29.185
We're all Austrian.

00:38:29.390 --> 00:38:33.793
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:34.028 --> 00:38:35.791
They're getting ready to...

00:38:37.465 --> 00:38:39.899
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:40.201 --> 00:38:45.104
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:45.306 --> 00:38:48.571
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:49.110 --> 00:38:50.577
Me? Why?

00:38:50.878 --> 00:38:52.436
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:52.880 --> 00:38:54.370
You're such a baby!

00:38:54.815 --> 00:38:57.716
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:38:59.954 --> 00:39:03.481
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:03.724 --> 00:39:07.091
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:07.728 --> 00:39:10.959
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:11.232 --> 00:39:15.293
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:16.003 --> 00:39:21.498
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:22.443 --> 00:39:26.379
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:26.580 --> 00:39:30.414
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:30.618 --> 00:39:34.247
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:34.488 --> 00:39:38.117
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:38.459 --> 00:39:42.293
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:42.496 --> 00:39:46.159
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:46.467 --> 00:39:49.800
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:50.004 --> 00:39:53.940
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:54.208 --> 00:39:57.974
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:58.379 --> 00:40:01.940
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:02.516 --> 00:40:06.680
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:06.987 --> 00:40:10.479
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:10.691 --> 00:40:14.559
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:14.795 --> 00:40:18.663
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:18.899 --> 00:40:22.335
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:22.570 --> 00:40:28.531
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:01.075 --> 00:41:04.408
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:04.612 --> 00:41:08.013
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:08.282 --> 00:41:11.513
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:11.752 --> 00:41:15.449
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:15.923 --> 00:41:19.086
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:19.293 --> 00:41:23.059
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:23.264 --> 00:41:26.722
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:27.034 --> 00:41:30.367
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:30.571 --> 00:41:34.098
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:34.375 --> 00:41:37.867
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:38.279 --> 00:41:41.612
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:41.882 --> 00:41:45.545
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:45.986 --> 00:41:49.581
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:49.823 --> 00:41:53.122
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:53.460 --> 00:41:57.157
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:57.398 --> 00:42:03.064
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:56.116 --> 00:43:57.549
Come in.

00:43:58.585 --> 00:44:00.212
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:02.556 --> 00:44:04.285
For your new dresses.

00:44:04.591 --> 00:44:08.584
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:08.862 --> 00:44:12.298
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:12.566 --> 00:44:16.058
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:16.303 --> 00:44:19.932
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:20.207 --> 00:44:22.266
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:22.543 --> 00:44:26.070
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:26.580 --> 00:44:28.980
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:29.983 --> 00:44:32.383
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:32.619 --> 00:44:35.315
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:36.156 --> 00:44:37.555
Whistles, orders.

00:44:37.825 --> 00:44:39.656
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:39.927 --> 00:44:43.454
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:43.964 --> 00:44:45.056
But that's so wrong.

00:44:45.899 --> 00:44:47.423
Oh, well.

00:44:47.634 --> 00:44:51.297
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:51.572 --> 00:44:52.834
Bu these are fine.

00:44:53.073 --> 00:44:54.734
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:54.942 --> 00:44:58.241
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:58.479 --> 00:45:02.506
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:02.783 --> 00:45:07.243
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:07.821 --> 00:45:12.417
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:13.594 --> 00:45:18.156
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:18.432 --> 00:45:21.333
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:21.535 --> 00:45:23.833
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:24.037 --> 00:45:27.268
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:28.709 --> 00:45:30.006
Yes.

00:45:30.277 --> 00:45:32.006
Well, good night.

00:45:32.212 --> 00:45:33.645
Good night.

00:45:52.065 --> 00:45:54.898
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:55.135 --> 00:45:58.002
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:58.238 --> 00:46:01.537
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:01.742 --> 00:46:04.870
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:05.078 --> 00:46:09.242
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:09.550 --> 00:46:12.383
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:14.154 --> 00:46:15.985
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:16.189 --> 00:46:20.182
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:20.394 --> 00:46:22.191
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:22.396 --> 00:46:24.921
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:25.432 --> 00:46:27.332
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:27.534 --> 00:46:30.094
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:30.837 --> 00:46:31.997
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:32.239 --> 00:46:35.675
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:35.943 --> 00:46:38.571
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:38.779 --> 00:46:41.771
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:42.082 --> 00:46:45.711
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:47.354 --> 00:46:50.380
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:56.463 --> 00:46:57.760
How did you climb up?

00:46:58.265 --> 00:47:01.393
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:01.602 --> 00:47:04.594
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:05.606 --> 00:47:07.267
Spiders?

00:47:10.978 --> 00:47:13.606
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:21.088 --> 00:47:24.785
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:25.459 --> 00:47:27.222
You could put this on.

00:47:28.962 --> 00:47:31.658
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:31.898 --> 00:47:35.425
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:36.737 --> 00:47:39.763
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:39.973 --> 00:47:42.066
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:12.539 --> 00:48:15.099
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:18.612 --> 00:48:20.876
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:21.114 --> 00:48:23.378
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:24.551 --> 00:48:28.783
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:33.193 --> 00:48:35.024
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:36.563 --> 00:48:38.531
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:38.832 --> 00:48:41.528
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:42.636 --> 00:48:46.970
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:53.046 --> 00:48:54.843
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:55.382 --> 00:48:58.579
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:48:59.686 --> 00:49:02.712
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:03.023 --> 00:49:04.854
It was Kurt's!

00:49:05.092 --> 00:49:07.686
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:10.497 --> 00:49:12.260
Why does it do that?

00:49:12.499 --> 00:49:16.333
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:16.570 --> 00:49:19.061
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:19.339 --> 00:49:21.603
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:21.875 --> 00:49:24.002
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:25.879 --> 00:49:30.077
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:30.283 --> 00:49:32.114
What kind of things?

00:49:32.886 --> 00:49:34.854
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:35.088 --> 00:49:36.180
Daffodils.

00:49:37.457 --> 00:49:38.856
Green meadows.

00:49:39.259 --> 00:49:41.523
Skies full of stars.

00:49:41.728 --> 00:49:44.925
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:45.132 --> 00:49:48.260
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:48.468 --> 00:49:51.631
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:51.905 --> 00:49:55.898
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:58.478 --> 00:50:01.276
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:01.548 --> 00:50:04.745
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:04.985 --> 00:50:07.920
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:08.155 --> 00:50:11.989
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:13.260 --> 00:50:15.990
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:16.263 --> 00:50:19.460
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:19.733 --> 00:50:22.793
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:23.069 --> 00:50:26.436
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:26.640 --> 00:50:28.335
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:28.575 --> 00:50:30.236
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:30.477 --> 00:50:32.741
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:32.979 --> 00:50:36.346
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:36.616 --> 00:50:43.454
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:44.191 --> 00:50:45.852
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:46.159 --> 00:50:48.093
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:48.795 --> 00:50:51.025
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:51.264 --> 00:50:52.925
Snakes!

00:50:53.200 --> 00:50:55.327
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:55.635 --> 00:50:56.761
Pillow fights!

00:50:57.037 --> 00:50:59.028
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:50:59.439 --> 00:51:01.805
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:03.310 --> 00:51:04.641
A good sneeze!

00:51:04.945 --> 00:51:06.674
Gesundheit!

00:51:06.980 --> 00:51:08.208
See what fun it is?

00:51:08.448 --> 00:51:11.383
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:11.651 --> 00:51:14.518
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:14.788 --> 00:51:17.780
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:18.024 --> 00:51:20.857
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:24.297 --> 00:51:27.130
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:27.367 --> 00:51:30.234
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:30.470 --> 00:51:33.405
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:33.673 --> 00:51:37.165
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:38.144 --> 00:51:39.634
Together.

00:51:39.913 --> 00:51:42.677
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:42.916 --> 00:51:45.817
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:46.052 --> 00:51:49.044
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:49.322 --> 00:51:52.587
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:52.893 --> 00:51:55.020
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:55.228 --> 00:51:57.196
Dog bites.

00:52:03.837 --> 00:52:05.065
Hello.

00:52:05.272 --> 00:52:09.436
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:09.743 --> 00:52:12.439
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:13.847 --> 00:52:14.836
You did, sir.

00:52:15.048 --> 00:52:19.246
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:20.553 --> 00:52:22.180
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:24.691 --> 00:52:26.181
Liesl?

00:52:26.426 --> 00:52:28.621
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:29.229 --> 00:52:30.958
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:31.231 --> 00:52:32.459
Yes?

00:52:33.266 --> 00:52:34.426
Well, I was...

00:52:34.701 --> 00:52:36.760
What she would like to say...

00:52:36.970 --> 00:52:39.871
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:40.073 --> 00:52:44.942
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:49.582 --> 00:52:50.981
Fräulein...

00:52:51.284 --> 00:52:55.311
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:56.423 --> 00:53:00.951
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:02.629 --> 00:53:05.120
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:05.632 --> 00:53:07.395
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:08.768 --> 00:53:10.133
Captain?

00:53:11.104 --> 00:53:15.006
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:15.275 --> 00:53:17.971
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:18.244 --> 00:53:20.405
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:20.613 --> 00:53:22.774
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:23.016 --> 00:53:24.779
And I'm their father.

00:53:25.352 --> 00:53:26.580
Good night.

00:53:50.844 --> 00:53:56.680
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:08.194 --> 00:54:11.721
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:11.965 --> 00:54:14.456
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:14.701 --> 00:54:18.000
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:18.204 --> 00:54:20.331
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:20.573 --> 00:54:27.502
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:51.504 --> 00:54:54.200
Children, over here. See!

00:54:57.844 --> 00:54:59.209
Come on.

00:56:22.262 --> 00:56:23.490
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:23.763 --> 00:56:25.663
Can we do this every day?

00:56:25.965 --> 00:56:29.162
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:29.502 --> 00:56:30.764
Every other day?

00:56:30.970 --> 00:56:35.600
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:35.808 --> 00:56:39.710
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:39.979 --> 00:56:41.810
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:42.015 --> 00:56:44.449
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:45.218 --> 00:56:46.810
Oh, I see.

00:56:48.154 --> 00:56:50.349
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:52.525 --> 00:56:54.152
All right, over here.

00:56:54.360 --> 00:56:55.793
What are we going to do?

00:56:56.029 --> 00:56:57.997
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:58.231 --> 00:57:00.199
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:57:00.466 --> 00:57:04.027
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:04.304 --> 00:57:06.465
We don't know any songs.

00:57:06.706 --> 00:57:09.368
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:11.044 --> 00:57:13.205
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:13.479 --> 00:57:15.208
But how?

00:57:19.519 --> 00:57:23.478
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:23.690 --> 00:57:27.057
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:29.194
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:29.429 --> 00:57:30.657
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:30.863 --> 00:57:35.197
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:35.435 --> 00:57:37.062
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:37.337 --> 00:57:38.668
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:38.905 --> 00:57:42.739
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:43.009 --> 00:57:44.772
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:45.011 --> 00:57:46.273
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:46.512 --> 00:57:50.448
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:51.117 --> 00:57:53.551
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:56.956 --> 00:58:00.619
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:00.860 --> 00:58:04.421
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:04.697 --> 00:58:08.463
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:08.735 --> 00:58:12.432
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:12.705 --> 00:58:16.471
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:16.776 --> 00:58:20.610
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:20.880 --> 00:58:23.815
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:24.284 --> 00:58:28.380
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:28.888 --> 00:58:32.449
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:32.725 --> 00:58:35.922
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:36.162 --> 00:58:39.461
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:39.732 --> 00:58:42.826
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:43.336 --> 00:58:46.794
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:47.006 --> 00:58:50.339
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:50.777 --> 00:58:53.644
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:53.913 --> 00:58:56.177
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:56.416 --> 00:58:59.852
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:59:00.119 --> 00:59:03.179
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:03.656 --> 00:59:06.853
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:07.126 --> 00:59:10.186
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:10.463 --> 00:59:13.694
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:14.000 --> 00:59:17.367
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:17.637 --> 00:59:20.265
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:20.473 --> 00:59:24.534
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:24.944 --> 00:59:28.038
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:28.481 --> 00:59:33.043
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:33.319 --> 00:59:36.550
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:36.823 --> 00:59:38.950
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:40.193 --> 00:59:45.688
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:45.898 --> 00:59:46.990
Can you do that?

00:59:47.200 --> 00:59:52.695
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:52.905 --> 00:59:58.571
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:58.878 --> 01:00:04.180
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:04.384 --> 01:00:06.147
Now, put it all together.

01:00:06.352 --> 01:00:12.985
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:13.226 --> 01:00:19.187
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:19.766 --> 01:00:22.360
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:22.602 --> 01:00:25.571
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:25.838 --> 01:00:27.100
Like this:

01:00:27.340 --> 01:00:33.904
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:34.180 --> 01:00:39.777
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:40.052 --> 01:00:41.019
Together!

01:00:41.220 --> 01:00:47.921
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:48.127 --> 01:00:54.794
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:55.201 --> 01:00:58.568
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:58.838 --> 01:01:02.035
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:02.308 --> 01:01:05.539
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:05.745 --> 01:01:08.805
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:09.048 --> 01:01:12.415
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:12.718 --> 01:01:15.983
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:16.189 --> 01:01:19.181
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:19.392 --> 01:01:23.260
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:40.847 --> 01:01:47.116
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:47.687 --> 01:01:54.183
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:54.760 --> 01:01:57.923
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:58.197 --> 01:02:01.724
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:01.934 --> 01:02:05.392
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:05.638 --> 01:02:08.801
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:09.075 --> 01:02:12.238
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:12.445 --> 01:02:15.642
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:16.249 --> 01:02:18.877
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:19.118 --> 01:02:23.077
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:23.289 --> 01:02:30.127
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:30.396 --> 01:02:34.890
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:35.134 --> 01:02:36.761
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:40.306 --> 01:02:46.108
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:46.312 --> 01:02:47.802
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:01.260 --> 01:03:04.354
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:04.597 --> 01:03:07.259
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:07.533 --> 01:03:09.694
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:09.969 --> 01:03:13.496
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:13.773 --> 01:03:16.037
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:16.642 --> 01:03:19.202
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:19.478 --> 01:03:22.003
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:22.281 --> 01:03:25.011
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:25.284 --> 01:03:27.878
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:28.187 --> 01:03:30.781
...and the price perfect.

01:03:31.157 --> 01:03:32.988
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:33.225 --> 01:03:37.218
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:39.865 --> 01:03:40.991
Listen.

01:03:43.336 --> 01:03:45.566
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:48.574 --> 01:03:50.201
They're good.

01:03:51.243 --> 01:03:52.870
Very good.

01:03:53.679 --> 01:03:56.341
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:56.549 --> 01:04:00.007
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:04:00.252 --> 01:04:04.552
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:04.757 --> 01:04:08.056
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:08.327 --> 01:04:12.696
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:19.739 --> 01:04:21.900
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:23.342 --> 01:04:25.674
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:40.893 --> 01:04:44.795
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:45.631 --> 01:04:48.191
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:48.467 --> 01:04:51.061
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:51.303 --> 01:04:55.262
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:55.541 --> 01:04:58.567
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:58.811 --> 01:05:02.975
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:06.752 --> 01:05:10.449
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:10.656 --> 01:05:13.489
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:13.793 --> 01:05:15.920
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:16.162 --> 01:05:20.155
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:20.433 --> 01:05:22.594
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:22.835 --> 01:05:24.427
How poetic.

01:05:24.637 --> 01:05:26.502
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:27.640 --> 01:05:32.771
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:32.978 --> 01:05:37.347
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:37.650 --> 01:05:41.347
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:41.654 --> 01:05:43.781
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:44.023 --> 01:05:46.321
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:49.695 --> 01:05:53.597
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:53.933 --> 01:05:55.867
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:56.135 --> 01:05:58.968
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:05:59.205 --> 01:06:02.470
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:03.209 --> 01:06:05.473
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:08.681 --> 01:06:12.617
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:13.285 --> 01:06:16.777
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:17.456 --> 01:06:21.790
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:22.027 --> 01:06:24.689
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:26.966 --> 01:06:28.228
Lovely...

01:06:29.235 --> 01:06:31.863
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:32.071 --> 01:06:34.904
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:35.341 --> 01:06:37.400
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:37.676 --> 01:06:39.507
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:39.712 --> 01:06:42.044
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:42.314 --> 01:06:45.545
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:47.386 --> 01:06:50.150
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:50.389 --> 01:06:55.156
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:55.361 --> 01:06:58.489
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:58.731 --> 01:07:00.562
But take all that away...

01:07:00.766 --> 01:07:05.203
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:05.871 --> 01:07:08.271
...searching, just like you.

01:07:13.379 --> 01:07:15.074
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:15.347 --> 01:07:16.871
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:17.116 --> 01:07:19.050
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:22.354 --> 01:07:25.380
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:25.591 --> 01:07:29.550
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:29.795 --> 01:07:32.457
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:32.698 --> 01:07:33.960
I hate thieves.

01:07:34.233 --> 01:07:37.532
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:37.770 --> 01:07:40.102
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:40.372 --> 01:07:43.933
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:44.410 --> 01:07:49.541
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:49.882 --> 01:07:51.873
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:52.284 --> 01:07:54.775
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:55.054 --> 01:07:57.545
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:57.790 --> 01:08:02.284
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:11.337 --> 01:08:12.736
Well?

01:08:13.639 --> 01:08:14.833
Well what?

01:08:15.074 --> 01:08:17.975
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:18.244 --> 01:08:20.235
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:20.479 --> 01:08:23.243
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:23.449 --> 01:08:25.007
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:25.317 --> 01:08:27.751
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:28.020 --> 01:08:31.615
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:31.924 --> 01:08:36.987
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:38.464 --> 01:08:42.594
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:42.835 --> 01:08:45.861
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:46.138 --> 01:08:49.369
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:49.642 --> 01:08:52.133
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:52.378 --> 01:08:54.642
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:54.847 --> 01:08:57.975
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:58.183 --> 01:09:00.151
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:09:00.352 --> 01:09:04.379
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:04.623 --> 01:09:08.184
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:24.476 --> 01:09:27.411
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:27.680 --> 01:09:29.705
I was just looking for...

01:09:30.582 --> 01:09:33.415
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:34.019 --> 01:09:35.714
Heil Hitler!

01:09:36.422 --> 01:09:37.912
Who are you?

01:09:38.190 --> 01:09:40.420
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:40.693 --> 01:09:43.423
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:48.500 --> 01:09:51.094
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:57.876 --> 01:10:01.277
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:01.513 --> 01:10:04.277
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:04.583 --> 01:10:07.245
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:07.519 --> 01:10:09.714
I have no political convictions.

01:10:09.955 --> 01:10:12.890
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:14.026 --> 01:10:16.187
You must help it.

01:10:26.472 --> 01:10:28.064
Hello?

01:10:30.709 --> 01:10:33.473
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:33.779 --> 01:10:37.647
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:38.484 --> 01:10:42.079
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:08.013 --> 01:11:10.504
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:11.316 --> 01:11:13.944
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:22.327 --> 01:11:24.989
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:34.106 --> 01:11:36.301
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:41.613 --> 01:11:44.605
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:56.562 --> 01:11:57.961
Straight line!

01:12:12.644 --> 01:12:15.044
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:17.649 --> 01:12:19.412
And these...

01:12:19.651 --> 01:12:21.243
...are my children.

01:12:22.354 --> 01:12:23.844
How do you do?

01:12:24.923 --> 01:12:29.656
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:34.666 --> 01:12:36.759
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:38.504 --> 01:12:42.065
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:52.284 --> 01:12:54.047
Now, fräulein...

01:12:55.954 --> 01:12:58.013
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:58.423 --> 01:12:59.890
Yes, captain.

01:13:00.192 --> 01:13:04.253
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:05.764 --> 01:13:10.258
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:10.736 --> 01:13:11.896
Yes, captain.

01:13:12.971 --> 01:13:14.302
I see.

01:13:14.873 --> 01:13:19.367
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:19.645 --> 01:13:21.704
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:21.914 --> 01:13:25.315
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:26.118 --> 01:13:28.245
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:28.453 --> 01:13:30.387
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:30.622 --> 01:13:35.082
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:35.294 --> 01:13:38.661
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:38.897 --> 01:13:40.558
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:40.766 --> 01:13:43.997
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:44.236 --> 01:13:47.000
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:47.272 --> 01:13:48.398
They don't complain.

01:13:48.640 --> 01:13:51.336
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:51.577 --> 01:13:53.135
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:53.345 --> 01:13:55.279
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:55.480 --> 01:13:57.004
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:57.249 --> 01:13:59.740
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:14:00.519 --> 01:14:02.680
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:02.955 --> 01:14:05.822
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:06.091 --> 01:14:09.151
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:09.428 --> 01:14:10.759
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:10.996 --> 01:14:14.261
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:14.499 --> 01:14:17.627
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:17.836 --> 01:14:19.360
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:19.638 --> 01:14:22.038
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:22.307 --> 01:14:25.504
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:25.777 --> 01:14:27.301
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:27.546 --> 01:14:31.642
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:33.185 --> 01:14:34.345
Fräulein.

01:14:35.654 --> 01:14:39.784
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:39.992 --> 01:14:42.483
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:45.130 --> 01:14:46.461
What's that?

01:14:48.200 --> 01:14:49.224
It's singing.

01:14:49.868 --> 01:14:52.666
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:53.639 --> 01:14:55.197
The children.

01:14:58.076 --> 01:14:59.407
The children?

01:14:59.978 --> 01:15:02.708
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:08.353 --> 01:15:14.383
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:14.660 --> 01:15:17.220
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:17.496 --> 01:15:22.934
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:23.201 --> 01:15:26.329
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:26.571 --> 01:15:28.004
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:28.240 --> 01:15:33.177
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:33.378 --> 01:15:38.008
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:38.283 --> 01:15:42.185
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:42.454 --> 01:15:45.389
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:45.691 --> 01:15:47.056
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:47.292 --> 01:15:51.729
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:51.930 --> 01:15:57.596
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:57.869 --> 01:16:02.363
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:02.574 --> 01:16:08.809
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:09.081 --> 01:16:12.778
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:13.051 --> 01:16:18.819
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:19.658 --> 01:16:23.890
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:24.129 --> 01:16:31.092
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:31.970 --> 01:16:37.169
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:37.409 --> 01:16:45.509
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:18.784 --> 01:17:20.547
Edelweiss!

01:17:24.523 --> 01:17:27.686
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:36.301 --> 01:17:37.859
Don't go away.

01:17:42.974 --> 01:17:44.373
Fräulein.

01:17:47.712 --> 01:17:48.906
I...

01:17:50.382 --> 01:17:53.180
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:54.920 --> 01:17:58.515
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:17:58.924 --> 01:18:00.391
You were right.

01:18:02.861 --> 01:18:04.761
I don't know my children.

01:18:06.064 --> 01:18:10.194
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:10.535 --> 01:18:14.403
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:15.740 --> 01:18:17.173
I'd forgotten.

01:18:19.911 --> 01:18:21.242
Fräulein.

01:18:23.748 --> 01:18:25.010
I want you to stay.

01:18:29.020 --> 01:18:31.750
I ask you to stay.

01:18:33.592 --> 01:18:37.084
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:37.696 --> 01:18:38.754
More than you know.

01:18:58.483 --> 01:18:59.814
Marta.

01:19:00.552 --> 01:19:01.780
Curtain!

01:19:04.456 --> 01:19:07.789
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:09.294 --> 01:19:12.559
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:14.065 --> 01:19:17.330
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:18.904 --> 01:19:22.135
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:33.652 --> 01:19:36.519
Marta. Marta!

01:19:38.924 --> 01:19:40.915
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:42.661 --> 01:19:46.119
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:47.599 --> 01:19:49.931
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:52.437 --> 01:19:55.702
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:57.042 --> 01:20:00.307
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:11.389 --> 01:20:14.517
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:16.161 --> 01:20:19.494
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:20.665 --> 01:20:24.066
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:25.570 --> 01:20:28.869
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:15.453 --> 01:21:18.718
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:20.258 --> 01:21:23.523
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:24.863 --> 01:21:28.299
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:29.768 --> 01:21:32.896
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:34.606 --> 01:21:36.233
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:39.210 --> 01:21:42.475
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:06.971 --> 01:22:08.563
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:08.773 --> 01:22:10.263
Very good!

01:22:12.077 --> 01:22:13.977
Wonderful!

01:22:14.579 --> 01:22:17.742
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:17.949 --> 01:22:19.974
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:20.185 --> 01:22:24.417
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:28.159 --> 01:22:29.820
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:32.330 --> 01:22:34.298
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:34.499 --> 01:22:36.490
They're your children, captain.

01:22:43.708 --> 01:22:46.006
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:46.277 --> 01:22:48.609
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:48.847 --> 01:22:51.941
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:55.053 --> 01:22:56.486
Attention, everyone!

01:22:56.688 --> 01:23:00.146
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:23:00.391 --> 01:23:02.689
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:02.961 --> 01:23:07.955
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:08.166 --> 01:23:09.997
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:10.235 --> 01:23:13.204
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:15.006 --> 01:23:18.203
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:18.910 --> 01:23:22.846
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:23.081 --> 01:23:25.481
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:25.683 --> 01:23:26.877
Tell us.

01:23:27.085 --> 01:23:30.543
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:30.822 --> 01:23:33.723
What a charming idea!

01:23:33.925 --> 01:23:35.722
Whose family?

01:23:36.594 --> 01:23:38.221
Yours.

01:23:38.429 --> 01:23:40.761
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:43.601 --> 01:23:46.593
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:46.871 --> 01:23:49.999
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:50.742 --> 01:23:53.074
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:53.344 --> 01:23:55.539
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:55.747 --> 01:24:00.548
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:01.219 --> 01:24:03.187
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:03.388 --> 01:24:06.380
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:09.194 --> 01:24:10.354
Who?

01:24:16.534 --> 01:24:17.728
Yes.

01:24:20.605 --> 01:24:22.539
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:23.374 --> 01:24:24.932
You, captain.

01:24:25.210 --> 01:24:26.404
Me?

01:24:27.245 --> 01:24:29.543
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:35.753 --> 01:24:37.880
No, no, no, no.

01:24:38.156 --> 01:24:40.215
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:40.425 --> 01:24:43.724
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:43.962 --> 01:24:46.829
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:49.767 --> 01:24:50.825
Well...

01:25:01.079 --> 01:25:03.240
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:03.514 --> 01:25:05.812
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:08.152 --> 01:25:10.279
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:11.856 --> 01:25:14.154
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:15.260 --> 01:25:21.460
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:21.699 --> 01:25:24.759
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:25.603 --> 01:25:28.970
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:29.173 --> 01:25:32.006
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:32.210 --> 01:25:36.044
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:36.314 --> 01:25:38.612
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:38.883 --> 01:25:43.013
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:43.221 --> 01:25:49.558
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:50.528 --> 01:25:54.225
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:54.465 --> 01:25:57.059
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:57.735 --> 01:26:05.005
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:09.380 --> 01:26:12.577
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:12.884 --> 01:26:16.376
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:16.587 --> 01:26:22.992
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:23.227 --> 01:26:26.754
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:27.031 --> 01:26:30.489
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:30.702 --> 01:26:33.193
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:33.438 --> 01:26:37.067
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:37.542 --> 01:26:39.669
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:39.877 --> 01:26:44.041
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:44.282 --> 01:26:51.347
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:51.589 --> 01:26:55.218
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:55.460 --> 01:26:58.122
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:58.730 --> 01:27:08.628
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:17.915 --> 01:27:21.578
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:21.786 --> 01:27:24.277
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:25.390 --> 01:27:27.881
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:28.126 --> 01:27:30.594
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:30.828 --> 01:27:33.797
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:34.065 --> 01:27:36.761
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:36.968 --> 01:27:39.334
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:39.637 --> 01:27:42.128
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:42.407 --> 01:27:44.637
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:44.909 --> 01:27:48.072
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:49.013 --> 01:27:50.310
Good night, Father.

01:27:50.515 --> 01:27:53.348
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:53.584 --> 01:27:55.142
Good night, Father.

01:27:58.122 --> 01:27:59.953
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:01.859 --> 01:28:05.022
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:37.562 --> 01:28:40.190
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:40.398 --> 01:28:43.526
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:44.836 --> 01:28:47.304
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:07.925 --> 01:29:11.361
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:18.436 --> 01:29:20.233
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:20.505 --> 01:29:21.836
I think they look ugly.

01:29:22.106 --> 01:29:23.937
You're just scared of them.

01:29:24.175 --> 01:29:26.405
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:27.011 --> 01:29:30.572
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:47.865 --> 01:29:49.890
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:50.101 --> 01:29:51.728
Nobody.

01:29:52.537 --> 01:29:54.437
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:56.908 --> 01:29:58.398
May I have this dance?

01:29:58.609 --> 01:30:01.100
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:07.885 --> 01:30:10.547
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:10.788 --> 01:30:15.725
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:20.131 --> 01:30:21.826
What are they playing?

01:30:22.066 --> 01:30:24.694
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:24.902 --> 01:30:28.065
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:28.272 --> 01:30:30.240
You remember. Please?

01:30:30.508 --> 01:30:32.442
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:32.677 --> 01:30:34.907
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:35.413 --> 01:30:38.246
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:39.183 --> 01:30:42.118
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:42.353 --> 01:30:45.015
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:45.323 --> 01:30:49.919
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:50.161 --> 01:30:52.823
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:53.030 --> 01:30:56.989
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:57.668 --> 01:30:59.363
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:30:59.604 --> 01:31:01.094
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:29.393 --> 01:32:31.258
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:33.431 --> 01:32:35.626
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:36.967 --> 01:32:39.060
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:41.772 --> 01:32:43.763
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:44.041 --> 01:32:45.941
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:46.143 --> 01:32:48.270
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:48.546 --> 01:32:49.877
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:50.114 --> 01:32:52.981
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:53.284 --> 01:32:54.444
Yes, come on!

01:33:01.292 --> 01:33:03.624
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:03.894 --> 01:33:06.920
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:09.834 --> 01:33:13.429
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:13.637 --> 01:33:15.662
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:19.844 --> 01:33:21.072
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:21.812 --> 01:33:25.908
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:40.030 --> 01:33:43.932
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:44.135 --> 01:33:47.866
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:48.139 --> 01:33:52.166
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:52.376 --> 01:33:54.810
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:55.045 --> 01:33:56.706
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:56.981 --> 01:33:58.209
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:58.449 --> 01:34:00.610
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:00.818 --> 01:34:02.183
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:02.453 --> 01:34:05.513
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:05.723 --> 01:34:11.025
<i>To you</i>

01:34:14.231 --> 01:34:18.133
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:18.335 --> 01:34:22.203
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:29.480 --> 01:34:32.813
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:33.484 --> 01:34:37.011
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:44.361 --> 01:34:48.161
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:48.432 --> 01:34:52.368
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:52.603 --> 01:34:55.037
- Yes?
- No.

01:34:59.376 --> 01:35:03.039
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:03.380 --> 01:35:07.339
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:07.551 --> 01:35:11.544
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:14.592 --> 01:35:17.686
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:17.928 --> 01:35:20.795
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:21.131 --> 01:35:24.123
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:24.401 --> 01:35:27.859
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:37.915 --> 01:35:43.649
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:43.888 --> 01:35:47.619
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:47.825 --> 01:35:50.225
<i>So long</i>

01:35:50.461 --> 01:35:53.021
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:53.230 --> 01:35:58.634
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:58.903 --> 01:36:04.239
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:04.942 --> 01:36:10.505
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:10.748 --> 01:36:17.620
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:17.821 --> 01:36:26.320
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:31.335 --> 01:36:34.099
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:34.338 --> 01:36:36.829
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:37.841 --> 01:36:41.834
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:42.112 --> 01:36:44.512
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:44.782 --> 01:36:47.717
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:47.952 --> 01:36:50.443
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:50.654 --> 01:36:52.554
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:52.823 --> 01:36:55.986
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:58.162 --> 01:37:00.892
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:01.699 --> 01:37:03.564
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:04.635 --> 01:37:06.125
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:09.740 --> 01:37:12.675
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:12.876 --> 01:37:13.740
I am, thank you.

01:37:14.011 --> 01:37:18.573
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:18.816 --> 01:37:22.252
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:22.653 --> 01:37:24.018
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:24.254 --> 01:37:28.020
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:28.926 --> 01:37:33.056
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:33.263 --> 01:37:35.663
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:36.734 --> 01:37:40.363
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:40.571 --> 01:37:43.506
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:44.041 --> 01:37:48.239
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:48.512 --> 01:37:52.209
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:52.416 --> 01:37:57.080
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:57.388 --> 01:37:58.412
You flatter me.

01:37:59.456 --> 01:38:03.358
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:11.101 --> 01:38:13.592
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:13.871 --> 01:38:15.429
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:15.906 --> 01:38:19.603
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:20.077 --> 01:38:24.207
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:24.448 --> 01:38:27.747
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:31.121 --> 01:38:32.952
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:34.291 --> 01:38:36.088
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:36.326 --> 01:38:39.727
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:39.963 --> 01:38:43.399
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:43.967 --> 01:38:46.401
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:46.637 --> 01:38:49.105
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:49.339 --> 01:38:52.968
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:54.578 --> 01:38:56.944
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:57.414 --> 01:38:58.676
Not at all.

01:38:58.916 --> 01:39:00.508
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:00.784 --> 01:39:02.342
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:02.986 --> 01:39:07.821
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:09.093 --> 01:39:11.527
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:12.463 --> 01:39:15.864
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:18.602 --> 01:39:20.194
But that's not true.

01:39:20.604 --> 01:39:24.096
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:24.374 --> 01:39:29.277
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:30.514 --> 01:39:32.209
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:32.483 --> 01:39:34.781
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:35.052 --> 01:39:37.020
Men do, you know.

01:39:38.021 --> 01:39:39.113
Then I should go.

01:39:40.457 --> 01:39:41.890
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:52.369 --> 01:39:55.805
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:57.574 --> 01:39:58.802
Yes.

01:39:59.810 --> 01:40:01.835
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:03.480 --> 01:40:07.041
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:13.824 --> 01:40:15.382
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:16.193 --> 01:40:18.991
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:49.026 --> 01:40:51.017
Champagne, darling.

01:40:51.428 --> 01:40:55.421
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:00.904 --> 01:41:03.805
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:04.041 --> 01:41:08.569
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:08.812 --> 01:41:11.440
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:11.915 --> 01:41:14.213
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:14.418 --> 01:41:16.113
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:16.320 --> 01:41:17.912
I thought of that.

01:41:18.155 --> 01:41:20.623
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:20.824 --> 01:41:23.725
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:48.658 --> 01:44:50.888
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:51.160 --> 01:44:52.650
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:53.896 --> 01:44:55.921
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:56.198 --> 01:44:57.825
Eight.

01:44:58.067 --> 01:44:59.898
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:01.003 --> 01:45:02.834
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:03.072 --> 01:45:05.267
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:09.912 --> 01:45:11.937
Isn't this fun?

01:45:13.349 --> 01:45:15.681
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:15.951 --> 01:45:18.112
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:18.421 --> 01:45:20.787
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:21.190 --> 01:45:22.418
Six.

01:45:24.894 --> 01:45:26.122
Two.

01:45:27.263 --> 01:45:30.232
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:30.466 --> 01:45:32.434
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:32.702 --> 01:45:34.693
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:44.880 --> 01:45:47.041
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:48.084 --> 01:45:49.711
Have some lemonade.

01:45:50.953 --> 01:45:52.386
There must be an easier way.

01:45:53.789 --> 01:45:57.054
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:57.993 --> 01:45:59.824
How do you plan to do it?

01:46:00.096 --> 01:46:02.121
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:02.398 --> 01:46:05.492
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:06.635 --> 01:46:08.899
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:10.239 --> 01:46:12.230
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:12.508 --> 01:46:14.305
I think he's in the house.

01:46:14.510 --> 01:46:17.070
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:17.313 --> 01:46:20.111
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:20.316 --> 01:46:21.214
What for?

01:46:21.417 --> 01:46:23.908
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:24.120 --> 01:46:27.988
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:28.257 --> 01:46:30.657
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:30.860 --> 01:46:33.829
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:34.096 --> 01:46:36.860
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:38.768 --> 01:46:41.430
Now, impress me.

01:46:45.441 --> 01:46:46.772
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:47.042 --> 01:46:49.510
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:50.546 --> 01:46:53.606
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:53.816 --> 01:46:56.148
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:56.385 --> 01:46:57.875
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:58.154 --> 01:46:59.781
All right, Liesl.

01:47:01.724 --> 01:47:07.128
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:07.363 --> 01:47:15.031
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:16.238 --> 01:47:21.301
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:21.544 --> 01:47:29.383
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:30.085 --> 01:47:35.489
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:35.724 --> 01:47:43.426
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:43.766 --> 01:47:46.394
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:46.702 --> 01:47:48.602
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:52.608 --> 01:47:56.510
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:56.912 --> 01:47:59.346
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:47:59.782 --> 01:48:02.046
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:02.351 --> 01:48:05.445
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:05.754 --> 01:48:10.453
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:11.193 --> 01:48:12.717
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:14.096 --> 01:48:16.121
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:16.532 --> 01:48:17.760
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:18.067 --> 01:48:21.525
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:22.271 --> 01:48:24.762
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:25.040 --> 01:48:27.201
She had to leave us.

01:48:27.443 --> 01:48:29.035
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:30.746 --> 01:48:33.442
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:33.649 --> 01:48:36.379
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:36.652 --> 01:48:38.449
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:38.754 --> 01:48:40.381
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:41.123 --> 01:48:43.114
Just too pink.

01:48:44.560 --> 01:48:47.654
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:54.303 --> 01:48:55.395
Well...

01:48:57.740 --> 01:49:02.973
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:03.312 --> 01:49:05.974
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:08.183 --> 01:49:10.310
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:11.420 --> 01:49:13.445
A new mother?

01:49:14.290 --> 01:49:17.418
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:17.626 --> 01:49:20.322
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:53.329 --> 01:49:55.797
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:27.763 --> 01:50:28.730
Yes, my children?

01:50:28.931 --> 01:50:31.331
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:31.834 --> 01:50:35.770
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:36.939 --> 01:50:38.930
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:39.708 --> 01:50:41.676
Oh, Maria.

01:50:43.579 --> 01:50:45.410
Come in, please.

01:50:49.284 --> 01:50:50.842
Wait here.

01:51:01.797 --> 01:51:04.960
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:05.234 --> 01:51:07.725
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:07.970 --> 01:51:10.564
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:10.873 --> 01:51:12.932
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:13.142 --> 01:51:15.042
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:15.277 --> 01:51:17.040
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:17.813 --> 01:51:20.714
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:20.949 --> 01:51:24.043
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:24.286 --> 01:51:26.777
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:26.989 --> 01:51:28.889
Some other time, dear.

01:51:29.158 --> 01:51:30.455
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:30.726 --> 01:51:33.786
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:34.430 --> 01:51:37.558
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:37.766 --> 01:51:39.393
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:39.668 --> 01:51:41.932
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:42.171 --> 01:51:45.902
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:48.677 --> 01:51:50.406
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:50.646 --> 01:51:52.841
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:53.082 --> 01:51:55.516
They want to see Maria.

01:51:55.784 --> 01:51:58.082
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:58.353 --> 01:52:02.346
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:02.624 --> 01:52:03.613
Poor child.

01:52:03.826 --> 01:52:06.795
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:07.029 --> 01:52:10.328
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:11.600 --> 01:52:14.660
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:14.937 --> 01:52:17.633
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:17.840 --> 01:52:19.501
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:25.013 --> 01:52:28.505
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:29.518 --> 01:52:31.782
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:37.993 --> 01:52:39.722
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:48.737 --> 01:52:51.001
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:53.041 --> 01:52:54.235
Reverend Mother.

01:52:54.576 --> 01:52:57.204
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:58.046 --> 01:53:00.014
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:02.518 --> 01:53:04.076
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:04.586 --> 01:53:06.383
Tell me what happened.

01:53:11.593 --> 01:53:12.924
I was frightened.

01:53:13.195 --> 01:53:17.655
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:17.900 --> 01:53:21.597
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:23.071 --> 01:53:25.164
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:25.407 --> 01:53:29.173
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:29.411 --> 01:53:34.110
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:34.383 --> 01:53:36.613
What is it you can't face?

01:53:38.587 --> 01:53:40.020
I can't face him again.

01:53:40.856 --> 01:53:42.380
Him?

01:53:43.959 --> 01:53:46.018
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:55.637 --> 01:53:57.264
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:02.711 --> 01:54:05.407
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:05.647 --> 01:54:07.114
I don't know. I...

01:54:07.649 --> 01:54:11.483
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:11.753 --> 01:54:14.415
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:15.490 --> 01:54:17.788
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:17.993 --> 01:54:19.551
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:19.928 --> 01:54:22.624
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:23.232 --> 01:54:25.894
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:26.101 --> 01:54:31.095
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:33.275 --> 01:54:36.073
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:36.945 --> 01:54:40.005
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:41.583 --> 01:54:46.282
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:46.521 --> 01:54:49.456
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:49.758 --> 01:54:53.592
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:53.795 --> 01:54:58.164
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:54:59.835 --> 01:55:01.700
No.

01:55:01.937 --> 01:55:03.802
You must find out.

01:55:05.540 --> 01:55:08.031
You must go back.

01:55:08.310 --> 01:55:10.278
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:10.479 --> 01:55:12.970
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:13.181 --> 01:55:17.140
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:17.352 --> 01:55:18.944
You have to face them.

01:55:19.521 --> 01:55:22.786
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:28.664 --> 01:55:32.964
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:33.201 --> 01:55:36.967
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:37.205 --> 01:55:41.972
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:42.210 --> 01:55:46.476
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:46.915 --> 01:55:51.375
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:51.653 --> 01:55:55.987
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:56.224 --> 01:56:00.593
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:00.862 --> 01:56:05.196
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:05.400 --> 01:56:08.494
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:08.737 --> 01:56:13.572
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:14.343 --> 01:56:17.744
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:18.013 --> 01:56:24.418
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:24.720 --> 01:56:29.020
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:29.257 --> 01:56:33.591
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:33.862 --> 01:56:38.424
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:38.633 --> 01:56:47.041
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:48.143 --> 01:56:51.635
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:51.947 --> 01:56:57.476
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:57.753 --> 01:57:01.245
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:01.490 --> 01:57:07.918
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:08.163 --> 01:57:12.600
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:12.834 --> 01:57:16.770
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:17.439 --> 01:57:22.069
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:22.477 --> 01:57:26.573
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:26.815 --> 01:57:36.816
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:39.361 --> 01:57:42.922
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:43.165 --> 01:57:45.258
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:46.935 --> 01:57:50.268
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:50.539 --> 01:57:53.975
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:54.776 --> 01:57:58.177
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:58.447 --> 01:58:00.506
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:01.883 --> 01:58:04.113
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:10.692 --> 01:58:14.651
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:18.233 --> 01:58:20.030
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:20.235 --> 01:58:21.497
You tell me.

01:58:22.838 --> 01:58:26.467
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:27.309 --> 01:58:31.973
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:32.214 --> 01:58:33.306
All afternoon?

01:58:33.548 --> 01:58:35.277
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:35.484 --> 01:58:38.385
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:38.653 --> 01:58:41.918
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:43.859 --> 01:58:47.226
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:48.730 --> 01:58:50.823
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:51.533 --> 01:58:54.229
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:59:00.075 --> 01:59:02.236
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:03.512 --> 01:59:04.706
- We...
- Well...

01:59:04.946 --> 01:59:07.710
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:07.949 --> 01:59:10.213
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:10.452 --> 01:59:13.250
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:13.455 --> 01:59:16.049
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:16.258 --> 01:59:17.850
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:18.093 --> 01:59:19.287
Very well.

01:59:19.561 --> 01:59:24.692
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:24.933 --> 01:59:28.869
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:29.104 --> 01:59:31.971
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:41.149 --> 01:59:43.947
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:44.219 --> 01:59:46.187
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:46.388 --> 01:59:48.322
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:48.557 --> 01:59:51.424
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:52.727 --> 01:59:55.821
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:56.264 --> 01:59:59.097
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

02:00:00.235 --> 02:00:04.137
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:04.573 --> 02:00:08.839
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:09.444 --> 02:00:10.911
Let's try it.

02:00:11.146 --> 02:00:13.808
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:14.115 --> 02:00:18.142
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:18.987 --> 02:00:21.581
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:21.790 --> 02:00:24.850
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:26.194 --> 02:00:32.155
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:32.434 --> 02:00:38.430
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:38.673 --> 02:00:40.698
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:41.876 --> 02:00:44.174
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:44.446 --> 02:00:47.540
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:47.816 --> 02:00:53.448
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:53.822 --> 02:00:56.985
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:57.192 --> 02:00:58.489
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:58.893 --> 02:01:02.158
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:02.397 --> 02:01:05.491
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:05.700 --> 02:01:07.827
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:08.336 --> 02:01:11.305
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:11.573 --> 02:01:13.837
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:14.042 --> 02:01:20.811
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:21.049 --> 02:01:24.075
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:24.319 --> 02:01:25.308
I missed you.

02:01:25.587 --> 02:01:27.714
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:29.257 --> 02:01:31.885
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:32.160 --> 02:01:34.321
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:35.563 --> 02:01:37.724
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:37.932 --> 02:01:40.924
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:41.169 --> 02:01:44.605
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:44.906 --> 02:01:49.605
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:49.844 --> 02:01:51.277
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:51.546 --> 02:01:53.537
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:53.882 --> 02:01:57.579
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:57.786 --> 02:01:58.844
Married?

02:01:59.187 --> 02:02:01.212
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:09.130 --> 02:02:10.688
Oh, I see.

02:02:12.534 --> 02:02:15.901
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:16.137 --> 02:02:18.196
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:20.408 --> 02:02:21.466
Good evening, captain.

02:02:22.944 --> 02:02:24.241
Good evening.

02:02:26.781 --> 02:02:28.612
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:28.917 --> 02:02:30.475
Dinner!

02:02:39.828 --> 02:02:44.561
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:45.567 --> 02:02:47.091
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:49.137 --> 02:02:50.297
Why did you?

02:02:50.505 --> 02:02:53.338
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:54.509 --> 02:02:57.603
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:58.847 --> 02:03:00.644
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:03.952 --> 02:03:06.182
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:06.421 --> 02:03:09.117
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:09.357 --> 02:03:10.483
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:13.027 --> 02:03:16.588
You are back to stay?

02:03:18.666 --> 02:03:21.999
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:17.692 --> 02:04:19.319
There you are.

02:04:33.708 --> 02:04:36.176
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:36.444 --> 02:04:39.743
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:40.181 --> 02:04:43.116
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:43.384 --> 02:04:45.375
Or was it the wine?

02:04:45.620 --> 02:04:47.451
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:50.024 --> 02:04:52.288
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:52.560 --> 02:04:55.290
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:55.597 --> 02:04:57.758
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:58.032 --> 02:05:01.627
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:01.870 --> 02:05:04.202
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:04.439 --> 02:05:06.703
...but you've already got one.

02:05:06.975 --> 02:05:09.910
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:10.144 --> 02:05:12.806
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:13.081 --> 02:05:15.481
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:15.783 --> 02:05:18.047
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:18.286 --> 02:05:21.050
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:23.224 --> 02:05:25.249
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:25.493 --> 02:05:27.085
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:27.295 --> 02:05:30.662
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:30.965 --> 02:05:33.798
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:34.068 --> 02:05:36.502
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:37.171 --> 02:05:38.433
Yes, Georg.

02:05:39.440 --> 02:05:40.771
It's no use...

02:05:41.976 --> 02:05:43.341
...you and I.

02:05:44.913 --> 02:05:48.144
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:49.484 --> 02:05:51.145
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:56.424 --> 02:05:59.154
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:06:00.028 --> 02:06:02.121
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:05.433 --> 02:06:10.461
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:11.372 --> 02:06:16.105
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:18.646 --> 02:06:21.137
You're much too independent.

02:06:21.449 --> 02:06:26.148
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:26.454 --> 02:06:29.446
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:31.626 --> 02:06:36.529
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:39.300 --> 02:06:41.200
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:41.402 --> 02:06:43.461
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:43.705 --> 02:06:46.196
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:51.579 --> 02:06:53.410
And somewhere out there...

02:06:53.715 --> 02:06:58.084
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:58.353 --> 02:06:59.581
...will never be a nun.

02:07:11.733 --> 02:07:14.065
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:39.794 --> 02:07:40.954
Hello.

02:07:46.768 --> 02:07:50.363
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:54.542 --> 02:07:56.806
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:57.245 --> 02:08:00.373
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:01.315 --> 02:08:02.646
Please.

02:08:07.789 --> 02:08:09.120
May I?

02:08:21.502 --> 02:08:26.235
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:27.408 --> 02:08:31.640
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:32.480 --> 02:08:37.144
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:38.820 --> 02:08:43.280
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:43.491 --> 02:08:45.618
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:46.260 --> 02:08:47.693
Is that all?

02:08:49.030 --> 02:08:51.191
And I missed the children.

02:08:51.532 --> 02:08:52.692
Yes.

02:08:53.968 --> 02:08:56.869
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:57.105 --> 02:09:00.939
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:01.142 --> 02:09:03.770
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:04.879 --> 02:09:06.642
Perhaps you might...

02:09:08.382 --> 02:09:09.610
Yes?

02:09:11.385 --> 02:09:16.687
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:17.458 --> 02:09:20.689
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:20.895 --> 02:09:25.559
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:29.637 --> 02:09:33.869
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:34.142 --> 02:09:35.473
Maria...

02:09:37.578 --> 02:09:41.070
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:43.484 --> 02:09:44.849
No.

02:09:45.153 --> 02:09:46.916
I don't understand.

02:09:49.323 --> 02:09:53.419
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:53.694 --> 02:09:57.152
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:58.332 --> 02:10:00.425
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:01.569 --> 02:10:06.097
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:08.676 --> 02:10:10.735
...in love with someone else...

02:10:14.115 --> 02:10:15.548
...can you?

02:10:50.418 --> 02:10:52.716
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:52.954 --> 02:10:56.390
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:04.799 --> 02:11:07.825
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:08.769 --> 02:11:11.169
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:12.840 --> 02:11:15.400
Is that why you came back?

02:11:19.447 --> 02:11:20.914
And have you found it...

02:11:21.916 --> 02:11:23.076
...Maria?

02:11:24.852 --> 02:11:26.843
I think I have.

02:11:29.590 --> 02:11:30.989
I know I have.

02:11:33.494 --> 02:11:35.155
I love you.

02:11:39.133 --> 02:11:40.998
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:44.372 --> 02:11:49.776
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:51.279 --> 02:11:56.512
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:58.386 --> 02:12:04.325
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:04.825 --> 02:12:10.627
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:11.565 --> 02:12:18.334
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:19.073 --> 02:12:25.069
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:25.713 --> 02:12:32.516
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:33.387 --> 02:12:41.021
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:42.263 --> 02:12:45.232
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:46.367 --> 02:12:50.235
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:51.072 --> 02:12:59.946
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:01.515 --> 02:13:11.015
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:11.892 --> 02:13:16.727
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:17.131 --> 02:13:21.033
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:21.268 --> 02:13:22.565
What?

02:13:23.904 --> 02:13:27.362
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:28.275 --> 02:13:30.266
Oh, my love.

02:13:34.048 --> 02:13:41.955
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:43.924 --> 02:13:49.760
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:51.132 --> 02:13:58.163
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:58.973 --> 02:14:06.675
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:07.848 --> 02:14:11.340
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:12.086 --> 02:14:15.112
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:15.356 --> 02:14:21.158
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:21.429 --> 02:14:23.659
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:26.767 --> 02:14:33.297
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:35.342 --> 02:14:47.982
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:54.695 --> 02:14:56.219
Maria.

02:14:58.065 --> 02:15:02.661
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:06.574 --> 02:15:09.134
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:57.651 --> 02:17:01.678
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:02.489 --> 02:17:06.186
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:07.161 --> 02:17:11.325
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:11.765 --> 02:17:12.754
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:13.000 --> 02:17:16.265
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:16.470 --> 02:17:21.032
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:21.475 --> 02:17:25.502
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:26.213 --> 02:17:30.513
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:30.884 --> 02:17:34.820
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:35.155 --> 02:17:40.149
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:40.527 --> 02:17:47.160
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:53.260 --> 02:19:54.818
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:57.431 --> 02:20:00.093
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:20:00.334 --> 02:20:03.633
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:03.937 --> 02:20:05.461
Heil Hitler.

02:20:06.373 --> 02:20:07.533
Heil Hitler.

02:20:07.841 --> 02:20:10.105
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:10.544 --> 02:20:14.139
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:14.381 --> 02:20:15.643
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:15.849 --> 02:20:18.010
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:18.285 --> 02:20:21.220
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:21.488 --> 02:20:23.183
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:23.690 --> 02:20:26.215
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:26.493 --> 02:20:28.358
When will the captain return?

02:20:28.896 --> 02:20:32.832
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:33.066 --> 02:20:37.901
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:38.172 --> 02:20:40.072
How many men do you know...

02:20:40.340 --> 02:20:43.639
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:44.545 --> 02:20:48.242
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:48.549 --> 02:20:50.915
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:51.151 --> 02:20:55.815
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:56.356 --> 02:20:59.814
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:21:00.060 --> 02:21:03.461
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:03.664 --> 02:21:05.359
Austria is the same.

02:21:06.233 --> 02:21:07.598
Heil Hitler.

02:21:09.770 --> 02:21:11.362
Heil Hitler.

02:21:13.040 --> 02:21:14.268
Come, let's go home.

02:21:14.508 --> 02:21:18.000
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:18.212 --> 02:21:21.579
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:21.782 --> 02:21:24.717
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:24.952 --> 02:21:27.682
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:27.921 --> 02:21:30.116
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:30.357 --> 02:21:33.258
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:33.460 --> 02:21:35.553
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:35.762 --> 02:21:40.358
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:40.567 --> 02:21:44.936
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:45.639 --> 02:21:47.266
There we go.

02:21:53.146 --> 02:21:56.604
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:56.817 --> 02:21:59.115
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:21:59.586 --> 02:22:02.054
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:02.256 --> 02:22:03.280
No.

02:22:03.490 --> 02:22:05.583
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:06.126 --> 02:22:08.287
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:09.229 --> 02:22:10.423
Rolfe!

02:22:11.431 --> 02:22:13.456
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:13.667 --> 02:22:14.759
Good afternoon.

02:22:15.168 --> 02:22:18.103
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:18.772 --> 02:22:20.637
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:20.841 --> 02:22:24.174
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:24.912 --> 02:22:27.472
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:27.681 --> 02:22:30.013
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:30.851 --> 02:22:33.342
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:33.820 --> 02:22:36.448
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:36.657 --> 02:22:39.148
And your father had better be too.

02:22:39.426 --> 02:22:40.916
But, Rolfe!

02:23:04.017 --> 02:23:05.678
Father!

02:23:05.953 --> 02:23:08.615
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:08.855 --> 02:23:11.653
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:11.858 --> 02:23:17.296
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:18.398 --> 02:23:19.695
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:19.900 --> 02:23:21.834
We couldn't get through.

02:23:22.135 --> 02:23:24.069
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:24.338 --> 02:23:26.363
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:26.673 --> 02:23:28.834
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:29.076 --> 02:23:31.510
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:31.712 --> 02:23:34.545
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:34.815 --> 02:23:39.013
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:39.219 --> 02:23:40.982
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:41.188 --> 02:23:42.815
I mean Mother.

02:23:43.223 --> 02:23:45.714
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:45.926 --> 02:23:48.053
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:48.328 --> 02:23:50.387
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:51.898 --> 02:23:54.230
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:54.901 --> 02:23:57.392
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:24:00.440 --> 02:24:01.839
We'll talk about this.

02:24:02.042 --> 02:24:06.342
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:06.613 --> 02:24:09.104
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:09.349 --> 02:24:14.082
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:14.287 --> 02:24:15.914
Max!

02:24:16.523 --> 02:24:19.356
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:19.626 --> 02:24:22.288
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:22.562 --> 02:24:24.257
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:24.464 --> 02:24:27.627
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:27.901 --> 02:24:32.201
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:32.439 --> 02:24:36.569
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:36.943 --> 02:24:40.208
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:40.447 --> 02:24:43.905
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:45.786 --> 02:24:47.447
You know, Max...

02:24:48.321 --> 02:24:51.586
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:54.261 --> 02:24:55.626
Father, I forgot.

02:24:56.463 --> 02:24:58.055
This is for you.

02:25:07.841 --> 02:25:11.834
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:12.112 --> 02:25:13.636
You must convince him.

02:25:13.847 --> 02:25:16.611
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:16.850 --> 02:25:20.149
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:20.420 --> 02:25:22.650
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:23.457 --> 02:25:26.824
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:31.998 --> 02:25:34.660
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:34.935 --> 02:25:37.665
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:37.871 --> 02:25:41.602
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:41.808 --> 02:25:42.604
Very much.

02:25:42.876 --> 02:25:46.175
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:46.880 --> 02:25:52.182
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:54.788 --> 02:25:56.847
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:57.290 --> 02:25:59.383
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:25:59.693 --> 02:26:01.024
It always does.

02:26:01.294 --> 02:26:04.855
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:05.065 --> 02:26:07.033
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:07.300 --> 02:26:09.495
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:09.736 --> 02:26:12.967
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:13.173 --> 02:26:17.405
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:18.078 --> 02:26:19.978
Do you really think so?

02:26:20.881 --> 02:26:24.817
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:25.085 --> 02:26:28.680
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:29.356 --> 02:26:33.190
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:33.426 --> 02:26:37.726
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:38.165 --> 02:26:39.860
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:40.333 --> 02:26:42.267
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:42.502 --> 02:26:46.370
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:46.606 --> 02:26:48.164
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:48.441 --> 02:26:50.568
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:50.777 --> 02:26:55.077
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:55.348 --> 02:26:59.250
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:26:59.519 --> 02:27:03.717
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:03.957 --> 02:27:08.360
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:09.296 --> 02:27:15.292
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:15.602 --> 02:27:19.902
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:20.106 --> 02:27:23.974
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:25.078 --> 02:27:30.448
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:31.284 --> 02:27:35.414
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:36.223 --> 02:27:41.456
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:41.895 --> 02:27:49.233
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:50.103 --> 02:27:58.738
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:01.147 --> 02:28:02.739
Liesl.

02:28:19.199 --> 02:28:20.530
What is it?

02:28:21.468 --> 02:28:22.833
Berlin.

02:28:23.303 --> 02:28:25.168
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:25.438 --> 02:28:27.963
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:28.208 --> 02:28:32.201
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:32.812 --> 02:28:36.805
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:37.050 --> 02:28:40.542
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:41.788 --> 02:28:45.554
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:51.731 --> 02:28:53.494
Get the children all together.

02:28:53.833 --> 02:28:57.030
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:58.004 --> 02:29:00.370
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:02.042 --> 02:29:03.703
...and this house...

02:29:06.046 --> 02:29:07.479
...tonight.

02:29:51.391 --> 02:29:53.791
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:54.060 --> 02:29:56.893
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:57.197 --> 02:29:59.859
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:30:00.100 --> 02:30:02.534
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:02.736 --> 02:30:04.033
You have no choice.

02:30:04.270 --> 02:30:07.103
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:07.807 --> 02:30:09.934
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:10.143 --> 02:30:13.579
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:17.217 --> 02:30:19.651
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:19.919 --> 02:30:23.446
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:23.656 --> 02:30:27.888
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:28.128 --> 02:30:33.065
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:30:59.859 --> 02:31:02.259
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:02.595 --> 02:31:04.859
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:08.635 --> 02:31:09.863
Karl.

02:31:11.838 --> 02:31:15.330
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:38.531 --> 02:31:40.328
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:43.703 --> 02:31:46.866
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:47.373 --> 02:31:49.500
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:49.709 --> 02:31:53.475
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:54.347 --> 02:31:56.815
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:57.050 --> 02:32:00.349
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:32:00.587 --> 02:32:03.055
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:03.323 --> 02:32:06.815
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:07.527 --> 02:32:11.054
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:12.198 --> 02:32:13.825
I have my orders...

02:32:14.067 --> 02:32:16.228
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:16.503 --> 02:32:18.698
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:19.839 --> 02:32:25.277
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:25.879 --> 02:32:27.608
You see, we...

02:32:28.181 --> 02:32:31.014
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:32.085 --> 02:32:34.110
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:34.420 --> 02:32:36.888
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:37.524 --> 02:32:40.391
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:40.593 --> 02:32:43.562
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:43.796 --> 02:32:46.697
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:46.933 --> 02:32:48.400
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:48.801 --> 02:32:52.931
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:53.306 --> 02:32:57.936
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:58.645 --> 02:32:59.976
Yes.

02:33:00.246 --> 02:33:02.737
Here, program.

02:33:07.754 --> 02:33:10.086
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:10.323 --> 02:33:13.588
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:13.826 --> 02:33:16.886
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:19.165 --> 02:33:22.965
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:23.803 --> 02:33:25.327
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:25.605 --> 02:33:29.006
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:35.248 --> 02:33:38.775
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:39.986 --> 02:33:41.510
Therefore...

02:33:42.355 --> 02:33:43.982
...you will sing.

02:33:44.924 --> 02:33:46.915
You will all sing.

02:33:47.293 --> 02:33:49.818
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:50.763 --> 02:33:54.199
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:54.934 --> 02:33:57.129
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:57.437 --> 02:34:00.600
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:01.874 --> 02:34:04.604
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:04.844 --> 02:34:08.678
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:09.549 --> 02:34:11.710
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:11.951 --> 02:34:14.442
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:15.355 --> 02:34:19.223
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:20.460 --> 02:34:21.950
Would we?

02:34:22.629 --> 02:34:23.789
No.

02:34:40.013 --> 02:34:43.176
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:43.383 --> 02:34:46.580
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:46.853 --> 02:34:50.311
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:50.523 --> 02:34:54.323
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:03.903 --> 02:35:06.064
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:11.944 --> 02:35:15.277
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:15.515 --> 02:35:18.746
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:18.951 --> 02:35:22.546
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:22.789 --> 02:35:24.120
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:24.390 --> 02:35:25.914
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:26.125 --> 02:35:34.931
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:56.923 --> 02:36:00.051
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:01.327 --> 02:36:05.889
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:07.300 --> 02:36:08.961
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:10.570 --> 02:36:12.128
...a love song.

02:36:14.107 --> 02:36:16.302
I know you share this love.

02:36:17.610 --> 02:36:21.307
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:34.093 --> 02:36:37.620
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:37.830 --> 02:36:41.027
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:41.300 --> 02:36:47.034
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:47.440 --> 02:36:50.500
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:50.777 --> 02:36:53.541
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:54.113 --> 02:36:59.210
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:36:59.986 --> 02:37:02.011
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:02.288 --> 02:37:05.883
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:06.125 --> 02:37:11.791
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:13.299 --> 02:37:15.790
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:16.035 --> 02:37:18.663
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:18.871 --> 02:37:24.867
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:29.382 --> 02:37:32.476
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:32.718 --> 02:37:34.049
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:41.427 --> 02:37:44.521
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:44.730 --> 02:37:47.597
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:47.834 --> 02:37:53.170
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:54.006 --> 02:37:55.974
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:56.175 --> 02:37:59.576
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:38:00.246 --> 02:38:06.242
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:06.719 --> 02:38:09.620
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:09.922 --> 02:38:12.686
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:13.292 --> 02:38:21.529
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:39.252 --> 02:38:40.810
I think it'll work.

02:38:41.554 --> 02:38:43.317
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:43.823 --> 02:38:46.257
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:49.662 --> 02:38:51.220
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:51.964 --> 02:38:54.626
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:54.901 --> 02:38:57.995
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:38:58.971 --> 02:39:01.496
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:01.774 --> 02:39:04.800
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:05.077 --> 02:39:08.274
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:08.514 --> 02:39:10.914
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:11.984 --> 02:39:15.977
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:16.255 --> 02:39:18.985
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:19.191 --> 02:39:22.752
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:27.433 --> 02:39:31.961
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:32.605 --> 02:39:34.869
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:42.114 --> 02:39:45.709
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:45.985 --> 02:39:49.318
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:49.822 --> 02:39:53.690
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:53.893 --> 02:39:56.327
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:56.529 --> 02:39:58.190
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:58.464 --> 02:39:59.453
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:59.732 --> 02:40:01.324
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:01.534 --> 02:40:03.331
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:03.569 --> 02:40:06.333
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:06.539 --> 02:40:11.704
<i>To you</i>

02:40:14.680 --> 02:40:18.207
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:18.484 --> 02:40:22.215
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:28.394 --> 02:40:31.989
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:32.198 --> 02:40:35.861
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:42.174 --> 02:40:45.769
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:46.012 --> 02:40:47.604
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:47.880 --> 02:40:49.541
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:55.921 --> 02:40:59.721
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:59.925 --> 02:41:03.292
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:03.562 --> 02:41:07.362
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:07.600 --> 02:41:13.300
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:13.539 --> 02:41:18.738
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:18.978 --> 02:41:26.146
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:57.950 --> 02:42:02.080
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:02.288 --> 02:42:04.848
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:05.491 --> 02:42:07.823
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:08.094 --> 02:42:12.690
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:12.965 --> 02:42:15.195
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:52.138 --> 02:42:56.074
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:24.036 --> 02:43:28.200
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:28.440 --> 02:43:31.534
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:43.923 --> 02:43:45.584
The family von Trapp.

02:44:00.206 --> 02:44:01.264
They're gone!

02:44:19.959 --> 02:44:21.392
Come with me.

02:44:25.231 --> 02:44:27.222
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:28.133 --> 02:44:30.328
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:31.070 --> 02:44:34.335
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:45.317 --> 02:44:47.012
Open this gate.

02:44:48.153 --> 02:44:49.745
Good evening.

02:44:52.258 --> 02:44:53.691
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:13.545 --> 02:45:14.807
Two men in there.

02:45:15.014 --> 02:45:16.879
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:17.116 --> 02:45:19.346
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:33.832 --> 02:45:37.393
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:37.670 --> 02:45:40.195
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:40.406 --> 02:45:42.306
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:42.508 --> 02:45:44.408
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:45.010 --> 02:45:46.671
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:46.879 --> 02:45:49.404
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:55.254 --> 02:45:57.552
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:58.857 --> 02:46:02.156
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:02.761 --> 02:46:04.752
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:05.030 --> 02:46:07.191
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:08.233 --> 02:46:09.598
Maria.

02:46:10.336 --> 02:46:12.930
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:13.172 --> 02:46:16.266
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:17.242 --> 02:46:18.334
Yes, Mother.

02:46:19.712 --> 02:46:21.873
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:33.959 --> 02:46:35.119
God be with you.

02:46:42.067 --> 02:46:43.625
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:43.869 --> 02:46:47.066
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:47.306 --> 02:46:50.298
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:50.576 --> 02:46:53.773
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:08.447 --> 02:49:09.675
Let's try the roof.

02:50:05.938 --> 02:50:08.168
Rolfe, please.

02:50:13.278 --> 02:50:14.768
No, wait.

02:50:24.590 --> 02:50:25.921
Maria.

02:50:26.992 --> 02:50:28.425
Children.

02:50:32.464 --> 02:50:35.490
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:35.867 --> 02:50:37.596
Put that down.

02:50:38.670 --> 02:50:41.969
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:43.675 --> 02:50:45.700
You're only a boy.

02:50:48.714 --> 02:50:52.377
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:54.152 --> 02:50:56.143
Come away with us.

02:50:57.389 --> 02:50:58.549
Before it's too late.

02:50:59.157 --> 02:51:01.489
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:03.795 --> 02:51:07.128
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:08.133 --> 02:51:09.691
I'll kill you.

02:51:11.570 --> 02:51:13.037
Rolfe.

02:51:31.423 --> 02:51:32.754
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:35.527 --> 02:51:37.222
Lieutenant!

02:51:37.496 --> 02:51:38.622
They're here!

02:51:38.830 --> 02:51:40.388
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:21.707 --> 02:52:23.368
Reverend Mother.

02:52:24.643 --> 02:52:26.474
I have sinned.

02:52:27.646 --> 02:52:29.807
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:31.450 --> 02:52:33.782
What is this sin, my children?

